{"content":[{"c":["CUSHI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Joab’s messenger sent to David to announce Absalom’s defeat (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.18.21-32","r":"2Sam.18.21-32","rawR":"2Sam.18.21-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.18.21-32","value":"2Sam.18.21-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 18:21-32"},"). However, the Hebrew word transliterated “Cushi” should more likely be translated “Cushite.” ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CushPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CushPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CushPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cush (Place)"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Jehudi’s great-grandfather. Jehudi was a prince in the court of King Jehoiakim of Judah in the time of Jeremiah the prophet (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.14","r":"Jer.36.14","rawR":"Jer.36.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.14","value":"Jer.36.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Father of the prophet Zephaniah (",{"href":"?bref=Zeph.1.1","r":"Zeph.1.1","rawR":"Zeph.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zeph.1.1","value":"Zeph.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zep 1:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Cushi","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 18:21-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.18.21-32","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.18.21-32","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.18.21-32"},{"anchorText":"Jer 36:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.14","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.14","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.14"},{"anchorText":"Zep 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zeph.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Zeph.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Zeph.1.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b5466845ddfcd9c31e4a3eca62e53